stem:
What is the determinant \(\left| \begin{matrix}
    bc & a & a^{2} \\
    ca & b & b^{2} \\
    ab & c & c^{2}
    \end{matrix} \right|\) equal to?

solution:
\(\left| \begin{matrix}
    bc & a & a^{2} \\
    ca & b & b^{2} \\
    ab & c & c^{2}
    \end{matrix} \right| = \frac{1}{abc}\left| \begin{matrix}
    abc & a^{2} & a^{3} \\
    abc & b^{2} & b^{3} \\
    abc & c^{2} & c^{3}
    \end{matrix} \right|\)\
    \(= \frac{abc}{abc}\ \left| \begin{matrix}
    1 & a^{2} & a^{3} \\
    1 & b^{2} & b^{3} \\
    1 & c^{2} & c^{3}
    \end{matrix} \right| = \ \left| \begin{matrix}
    1 & a^{2} & a^{3} \\
    1 & b^{2} & b^{3} \\
    1 & c^{2} & c^{3}
    \end{matrix} \right|\)

